{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"504797","self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/504797","key":"MC-303455","renderedFields":{"summary":null,"issuetype":null,"watches":null,"customfield_10070":null,"customfield_10061":"","created":"21/Oct/25 11:50 AM","customfield_10050":"","customfield_10051":null,"description":"<p>As of snapshot 25w43a, Minecraft now runs on Wayland natively instead of XWayland on Linux. This comes with unfortunate side effects. One is the cursor no longer being centered when opening a container or menu.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><b>Steps to reproduce the issue</b><br>\n1. Make sure you are using Wayland and not X11<br>\n2. Launch snapshot 25w43a<br>\n3. Join a world and open the inventory, any other container or press ESC to open the pause menu<br>\n4. Move around the cursor and close the menu or container<br>\n5. Reopen the menu or container</p>\n\n\n<p><b>Expected result</b><br>\nThe cursor will always center like it did prior 25w43a.</p>\n\n\n<p><b>Actual result</b><br>\nThe cursor does not center.</p>\n","customfield_10054":null,"fixVersions":null,"customfield_10055":null,"resolution":null,"customfield_10047":null,"customfield_10048":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10049":null,"attachment":[{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/536949","id":"536949","filename":"image-20251021-190758.png","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","24x24":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","16x16":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","32x32":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png"},"displayName":"muzikbike","active":true,"timeZone":"Europe/Dublin","accountType":"customer"},"created":"21/Oct/2